# TLS in front of the agent front (`serve`) with Caddy and Let's Encrypt.
# Exactly what the phase-5 smoke ran on a VPS (docs/smoke-agent-pool.md), with
# the host name replaced: put your DNS name where <your-host> stands, and point
# that name at the host first -- the certificate is issued over HTTP-01 on :80.
#
# Why https_port is not 443: on the smoke host 443 already belonged to another
# service. Any free port works; the agent's address then carries it
# (https://<your-host>:8443). If 443 is free, drop both global options below
# and the ":8443" from the site address.
#
# Why disable_tlsalpn_challenge: the TLS-ALPN challenge is answered on 443,
# which Caddy does not own here; HTTP-01 on :80 is the one it can answer.
#
# reverse_proxy keeps the Host header, so `serve` sees the public host name --
# which is why `serve.publicUrl` (MCPCUT_SERVE_PUBLIC_URL) must be exactly this
# address: `setup` derives the Host allow-list from it.
{
	http_port 80
	https_port 8443
}

<your-host>:8443 {
	tls {
		issuer acme {
			disable_tlsalpn_challenge
		}
	}
	reverse_proxy serve:8090
}
